# Shell scripts run on macOS and must keep LF line endings wherever they are checked out.
*.sh text eol=lf
bin/agent-ha-bridge text eol=lf

# The reply card is published into Home Assistant byte for byte - install.ps1 copies
# the working tree and Get-BridgeInlineReplyCardUrl base64s exactly those bytes - and
# the publication fence compares their SHA-256. So the line endings a checkout happens
# to use are part of the published artifact. With core.autocrlf on, a Windows working
# copy hashes differently from the LF bytes git stores and every release download
# carries, and the fence sees one CARD_VERSION with two contents: the conflict it is
# built to refuse. That is not a conflict anybody can resolve, because bumping the
# version produces the same two hashes one version later, and it paused publication
# indefinitely while the dashboard went on rendering against whichever build got in
# first - two Send buttons and answers that could never be confirmed (#110).
frontend/agent-bridge-reply-card.js text eol=lf
